# Time in a system

This is a sample post for previewing the blog layout and its generated network artwork.

Dates, ordering and the surprising complexity of deciding what came first.

## A closer look

A useful experiment starts with something small enough to inspect. Change one
part, keep the rest steady, and take a moment to look at what happened. Sometimes
the most interesting detail is a gap, a cluster, or a connection that was easy
to miss at first.

The network above belongs to this post's URL. Its arrangement should stay the
same when you reload this page, while other sample posts have their own shapes,
colours and spacing. Open a few articles to compare their silhouettes.

## Notes from the experiment

- Look at how the title wraps on a narrow screen.
- Compare the density of branches on either side of the heading.
- Follow the article back to the listing and try another sample.

> A small change is easier to understand when there is something steady to compare it with.

## Next steps

These paragraphs are placeholder content for checking reading width, heading
